# The `agent-goals` recording rules — ADR-102's goal registry arithmetic — lifted VERBATIM out of
# prometheusrule.yaml (comments stripped, the manifest is their one home). This is the rules file
# that agent-goals.promtool-test loads. Not a manifest and not applied to anything: `promtool test
# rules` needs upstream-format rules (top-level `groups:`), and a PrometheusRule keeps them under
# `.spec`, so the CR cannot be loaded directly. Named .promtool-rules rather than .yaml on purpose
# — manifest-lint kubeconforms EVERY *.yaml under argocd/resources and a non-manifest there would
# fail it.
#
# The THIRD fixture over github-exporter's rule file (queued-age.promtool-* was first, FU-150/#284;
# loop-health.promtool-* second, #331) and the first over a RECORDING group. It exists because
# #348 found goal_budget_ratio and goal_budget_remaining_usd empty for every goal since #209 —
# a `sum by (…)` aggregate divided by a raw scrape, so the plain match never had a pair to match.
#
# ✅ DRIFT-PINNED, unlike loop-health.promtool-rules: `devbox run exporter-self-test` compares the
# three `agent-goals` record blocks below against prometheusrule.yaml line for line and fails if
# they diverge (github-exporter.py, record_rule()). That pin is the whole reason this copy is
# allowed to exist — the hazard it closes is homelab#337's: a stale copy tests the OLD expr and
# passes VACUOUSLY, which is a green that saw nothing (the FU-125/FU-108 class). Re-copy after
# editing a rule:
#
#   yq -o=json '{"groups": [.spec.groups[] | select(.name == "agent-goals")]}' argocd/resources/github-exporter/prometheusrule.yaml | yq -P '.'
#
# ONE LINE on purpose — yq 4.x's lexer rejects a newline inside the expression ("lexer: invalid
# input text"), so a pretty-wrapped form does not run as written (homelab#344, same constraint
# stated in loop-health.promtool-rules and agent-router.promtool-rules). Verified by RUNNING the
# line above on 2026-08-12. ⚠ Two things it does NOT do: it re-emits `goal_spent_usd`'s folded
# `>-` expr as a literal `|-` block (re-fold it by hand, or the drift pin's line comparison trips
# on formatting rather than meaning), and it regenerates the `agent-goals` group ONLY — the two
# witness groups at the bottom are not in the CR and must survive the re-copy.
groups:
  - name: agent-goals
    rules:
      - record: goal_spent_usd
        expr: >-
          sum by (owner, project, stack, goal) (
            sum by (project, issue) (agent_run_cost_usd)
            * on (project, issue) group_right () goal_descendant_info
          )
      - record: goal_budget_ratio
        expr: goal_spent_usd / max by (owner, project, stack, goal) (goal_budget_usd)
      - record: goal_budget_remaining_usd
        expr: max by (owner, project, stack, goal) (goal_budget_usd) - goal_spent_usd

  # ── regression witness: the exprs exactly as they shipped from #209 to #348 ────────────────────
  # NOT a proposal and not deployed — the pre-fix forms, kept runnable so the fixture can EXECUTE
  # the contrast instead of asserting it in prose (the #310/#328/#345 shape). Every case below that
  # asserts a shipped ratio also asserts these EMPTY at the same eval time; that pairing is what
  # attributes the fix to the join and not to the fixture's input.
  #
  # These read goal_spent_usd, which the group above records — group order in this file is
  # evaluation order, so the aggregate exists by the time these run.
  - name: regression-witness-pre-348
    rules:
      - record: goal_budget_ratio_pre348
        expr: goal_spent_usd / goal_budget_usd
      - record: goal_budget_remaining_usd_pre348
        expr: goal_budget_usd - goal_spent_usd

  # ── the REJECTED alternative is deliberately NOT a group here ─────────────────────────────────
  # #348 offered two working shapes and left the choice to the PR. The one not taken is an explicit
  #
  #     goal_spent_usd / on (owner, project, stack, goal) group_left () goal_budget_usd
  #
  # which returns the same three series as the shipped rule on a steady-state scrape and parts
  # company with it on a pod roll (agent-goals.promtool-test case 3). It is not carried here as a
  # fourth group because a rule that ERRORS cannot live in a green fixture: `promtool test rules`
  # reports a rule-evaluation error at every evaluation, asserted or not, and fails the whole run.
  # Adding it back and re-running yields, verbatim (measured 2026-08-12):
  #
  #   FAILED: rule: goal_budget_ratio_group_left, time: 8m0s, err: found duplicate series for the
  #   match group {goal="29", owner="teststuffstash", project="circles", stack="circles"} on the
  #   right hand-side of the operation: […pod="…-kcmdn"…, …pod="…-p2xqz"…]; many-to-many matching
  #   not allowed: matching labels must be unique on one side
  #
  # …which is the failure itself, not a description of it: a recording rule that errors records
  # NOTHING, for every goal in the rule, not just the doubled one. What CI holds standing instead
  # is the PRECONDITION — case 3 asserts that a surge really does put two goal_budget_usd series in
  # one match group, and that `max by (…)` really does collapse them to one.
